# EXAMPLE lane declaration (synthetic Testburg vocabulary — see
# cabinet/fixtures/testburg/README.md; everything here is fiction). Second of
# the two shipped example lanes: together with bakery-site.yml.example it
# models a multi-lane declaration set (the resolvers return a SORTED, deduped
# enum — file order never matters). Copy to
# instance/config/contexts/<your-lane>.yml and edit; the filename minus .yml
# must equal the slug. `active:` gates activation only — it never filters a
# lane out of the resolver enum (see bakery-site.yml.example for the full
# model notes).
slug: newsletter
name: Newsletter
capacity: work
description: |
  Ada Testburg's newsletter lane (synthetic example). The weekly bakery
  newsletter product. Declared-but-inactive lanes stay enumerable so shared
  code sees the same lane universe the Captain declared.
active: false
